<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 1 ══════════════════ -->
<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>
  LearnHub is a full-featured, web-based Learning Management System (LMS) built with the Laravel 11 framework.
  The platform is designed to support three distinct user roles — <strong>administrators</strong>, <strong>teachers</strong>,
  and <strong>students</strong> — each with a tailored experience and permission set.
</p>
<p>
  Students can browse the course catalog, enroll in courses, access lesson content, and submit reviews.
  Teachers are assigned to courses by administrators. Administrators have full control over the platform
  through a dedicated management panel, including the ability to manage courses, lessons, users, enrollments,
  teacher assignments, and notifications.
</p>
<p>
  The system enforces email verification for all registered users before granting access to protected
  functionality, and maintains a clean separation between the public-facing guest experience and the
  authenticated user experience.
</p>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 2 ══════════════════ -->
<h2>2. Technology Stack</h2>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Layer</th>
    <th>Technology</th>
    <th>Details</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Backend Framework</strong></td>
    <td>Laravel 11</td>
    <td>MVC architecture, Eloquent ORM, Blade templating, middleware</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Language</strong></td>
    <td>PHP 8.2+</td>
    <td>Typed properties, match expressions, named arguments</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Database</strong></td>
    <td>MySQL</td>
    <td>Accessed via Laravel migrations and Eloquent ORM</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Admin / User UI</strong></td>
    <td>Bootstrap 5.3</td>
    <td>Dark theme, custom CSS variables, responsive grid</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Auth UI</strong></td>
    <td>Tailwind CSS + Vite</td>
    <td>Custom split-panel design with inline styles</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Fonts</strong></td>
    <td>Figtree (Google / Bunny)</td>
    <td>Used across authentication pages</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Local Server</strong></td>
