    <td>Development environment on Windows</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 3 ══════════════════ -->
<h2>3. Database Design and Tables</h2>
<p>The database consists of six core tables covering users, course content, enrollments, teacher assignments, and reviews.</p>

<h3>3.1 Users Table</h3>
<p>Stores all platform users. The <code>role</code> column differentiates between admins, teachers, and students.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>BIGINT (PK)</td><td>Auto-incrementing primary key</td></tr>
  <tr><td>name</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>User's full name</td></tr>
  <tr><td>email</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>Unique email address</td></tr>
  <tr><td>password</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>Bcrypt-hashed password</td></tr>
  <tr><td>role</td><td>VARCHAR(50)</td><td>Values: admin, teacher, user</td></tr>
  <tr><td>email_verified_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>NULL until email is verified</td></tr>
  <tr><td>remember_token</td><td>VARCHAR(100)</td><td>Used for "remember me" sessions</td></tr>
  <tr><td>created_at / updated_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>Laravel timestamps</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>3.2 Courses Table</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>BIGINT (PK)</td><td>Primary key</td></tr>
  <tr><td>title</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>Course title</td></tr>
  <tr><td>description</td><td>TEXT</td><td>Detailed course description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>img_path</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>Path to the course thumbnail image</td></tr>
  <tr><td>created_at / updated_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>Laravel timestamps</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>3.3 Lessons Table</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>BIGINT (PK)</td><td>Primary key</td></tr>
  <tr><td>course_id</td><td>BIGINT (FK)</td><td>References courses.id</td></tr>
  <tr><td>title</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>Lesson title</td></tr>
  <tr><td>description</td><td>TEXT</td><td>Lesson summary or objectives</td></tr>
  <tr><td>content</td><td>TEXT</td><td>Full lesson text content</td></tr>
  <tr><td>video_path</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>Path or URL to lesson video</td></tr>
  <tr><td>created_at / updated_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>Laravel timestamps</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>3.4 Enrollments Table (Pivot)</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>BIGINT (PK)</td><td>Primary key</td></tr>
  <tr><td>user_id</td><td>BIGINT (FK)</td><td>References users.id (student)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>course_id</td><td>BIGINT (FK)</td><td>References courses.id</td></tr>
  <tr><td>created_at / updated_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>Laravel timestamps</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>3.5 Course_Teacher Table (Pivot)</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>BIGINT (PK)</td><td>Primary key</td></tr>
  <tr><td>user_id</td><td>BIGINT (FK)</td><td>References users.id (teacher)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>course_id</td><td>BIGINT (FK)</td><td>References courses.id</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>3.6 Reviews Table</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>BIGINT (PK)</td><td>Primary key</td></tr>
  <tr><td>course_id</td><td>BIGINT (FK)</td><td>References courses.id</td></tr>
  <tr><td>user_id</td><td>BIGINT (FK)</td><td>References users.id (reviewer)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>rating</td><td>TINYINT</td><td>Numeric rating (e.g. 1–5)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>comment</td><td>TEXT</td><td>Written review text</td></tr>
  <tr><td>created_at / updated_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>Laravel timestamps</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 4 ══════════════════ -->
<h2>4. Model Relationships</h2>
<p>All relationships are implemented using Laravel Eloquent ORM.</p>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Model</th>
    <th>Relationship</th>
    <th>Target</th>
    <th>Type</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>User</td>
    <td>enrolledCourses()</td>
    <td>Course</td>
    <td>Many-to-Many via <em>enrollments</em></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>User</td>
    <td>teachingCourses()</td>
    <td>Course</td>
    <td>Many-to-Many via <em>course_teacher</em></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>User</td>
    <td>reviews()</td>
    <td>Review</td>
    <td>Has Many</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Course</td>
    <td>lessons()</td>
    <td>Lesson</td>
    <td>Has Many</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Course</td>
    <td>enrolledBy()</td>
    <td>User</td>
    <td>Many-to-Many via <em>enrollments</em></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Course</td>
    <td>teachedBy()</td>
    <td>User</td>
    <td>Many-to-Many via <em>course_teacher</em></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Course</td>
    <td>reviews()</td>
    <td>Review</td>
    <td>Has Many</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Lesson</td>
    <td>course()</td>
    <td>Course</td>
    <td>Belongs To</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Review</td>
    <td>course()</td>
    <td>Course</td>
    <td>Belongs To</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Review</td>
    <td>user()</td>
    <td>User</td>
    <td>Belongs To</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 5 ══════════════════ -->
<h2>5. Authentication &amp; Security</h2>

<h3>5.1 Registration Flow</h3>
<p>
  When a new user completes the registration form, the system creates their account, logs them in
  automatically, and immediately redirects them to the <strong>email verification page</strong>.
  Access to all protected routes is blocked until the email is confirmed.
</p>

<h3>5.2 Login Flow</h3>
<p>
  Upon successful login, the system checks whether the user's email is verified:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>If <strong>not verified</strong> → redirected to the email verification notice page.</li>
  <li>If <strong>verified and role is admin</strong> → redirected to the Admin Courses dashboard.</li>
  <li>If <strong>verified and role is user</strong> → redirected to the Home page.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5.3 Email Verification</h3>
<p>
  The <code>User</code> model implements the <code>MustVerifyEmail</code> interface. All admin, user,
  and profile routes are protected with the <code>verified</code> middleware. Unverified users can
  only access the verification notice page and request a resend of the verification email.
  After clicking the verification link, users are redirected to the home page.
</p>

<h3>5.4 Middleware</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Middleware</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Applied To</th></tr>
  <tr><td>auth</td><td>Require authenticated session</td><td>All protected routes</td></tr>
  <tr><td>verified</td><td>Require confirmed email address</td><td>Admin, user, and profile routes</td></tr>
  <tr><td>admin</td><td>Restrict access to admin role only</td><td>All /admin/* routes</td></tr>
  <tr><td>guest</td><td>Redirect authenticated users away from auth pages</td><td>Login, register, password reset</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>5.5 Password Management</h3>
<p>
  Users can update their password from the profile settings page. The system validates the current
  password before accepting a new one. Password reset via email is also available from the login page.
  All passwords are hashed using bcrypt via Laravel's built-in hashing facilities.
</p>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 6 ══════════════════ -->
<h2>6. System Features by Role</h2>

<h3>6.1 Guest (Unauthenticated)</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Browse the home page freely</li>
  <li>Access the login and registration pages</li>
  <li>Request a password reset link</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.2 Student (Authenticated + Verified)</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Browse and search the full course catalog</li>
  <li>View course detail pages including lessons and reviews</li>
  <li>Enroll in and withdraw from courses</li>
  <li>Access lesson content for enrolled courses</li>
  <li>Submit and manage course reviews (rating + comment)</li>
  <li>View personal enrollment history ("My Courses")</li>
  <li>Update profile information (name, email)</li>
  <li>Change account password</li>
  <li>Delete account</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.3 Administrator (Authenticated + Verified + Admin Role)</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Access the admin dashboard with platform statistics (total courses, users, lessons, enrollments)</li>
  <li>Full CRUD management of courses (create, view, edit, delete)</li>
  <li>Full CRUD management of lessons</li>
  <li>Full CRUD management of users</li>
  <li>Manage student enrollments per course</li>
  <li>Assign and remove teachers from courses</li>
  <li>Search functionality across courses, lessons, and users</li>
  <li>View and manage admin notifications</li>
  <li>Update admin profile information and password</li>
</ul>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 7 ══════════════════ -->
<h2>7. Controllers Overview</h2>

<h3>7.1 Admin Controllers</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Controller</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Admin\DashboardController</td><td>Platform statistics and admin home view</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Admin\CourseController</td><td>CRUD for courses, search, image upload</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Admin\LessonController</td><td>CRUD for lessons, search, video management</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Admin\UserController</td><td>CRUD for users, role management, search</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Admin\EnrollmentController</td><td>Assign and remove student enrollments</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Admin\TeacherController</td><td>Assign teachers to courses</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Admin\ProfileController</td><td>Admin profile view</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Admin\NotificationController</td><td>View, mark-read, and manage notifications</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>7.2 User Controllers</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Controller</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr>
  <tr><td>User\CourseController</td><td>Browse and search course catalog</td></tr>
  <tr><td>User\EnrollmentController</td><td>Enroll, withdraw, and view enrolled courses</td></tr>
  <tr><td>User\ReviewController</td><td>Create and submit course reviews</td></tr>
  <tr><td>ProfileController</td><td>Edit profile info; role-aware redirect after save</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>7.3 Auth Controllers</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Controller</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Auth\RegisteredUserController</td><td>Registration form + redirect to verify-email</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Auth\AuthenticatedSessionController</td><td>Login + verification check + role-based redirect</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Auth\VerifyEmailController</td><td>Handle email verification link + redirect to home</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Auth\PasswordController</td><td>Update password from profile</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Auth\PasswordResetLinkController</td><td>Send password reset email</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Auth\NewPasswordController</td><td>Reset password via signed link</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 8 ══════════════════ -->
<h2>8. Pages and Views</h2>

