<h2>9. UI Design System</h2>

<h3>9.1 Color Palette</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Token</th><th>Hex Value</th><th>Usage</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Page Background</td><td>#0f172a</td><td>Main body background across all pages</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Card / Panel</td><td>#1e293b</td><td>Card backgrounds, navbars</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Card Header</td><td>#253047</td><td>Table headers, card header sections</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Admin Primary</td><td>#818cf8</td><td>Admin buttons, links, badges (indigo)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>User Primary</td><td>#38bdf8</td><td>User-facing buttons, links (sky blue)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Auth Accent</td><td>#a5b4fc</td><td>Auth pages logo text, feature dots</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Danger</td><td>#ef4444</td><td>Delete actions, error states</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Success</td><td>#34d399</td><td>Success states, save confirmations</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Muted Text</td><td>#94a3b8</td><td>Secondary text, placeholders, labels</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>9.2 Auth Page Layout</h3>
<p>
  The login and registration pages use a <strong>split-panel design</strong>:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Left panel</strong> (visible on desktop ≥ 1024px): Dark indigo gradient background with the LearnHub logo, a headline, subline, and four platform feature bullet points. Decorative blurred circles add depth.</li>
  <li><strong>Right panel</strong>: Dark <code>#0f172a</code> background with a raised <code>#1e293b</code> card containing the form. On mobile, the left panel is hidden and a compact logo appears above the card.</li>
</ul>

<h3>9.3 Profile Page Design</h3>
<p>
  Profile pages (shared between admin and user) are divided into three Bootstrap cards:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Profile Information</strong> — Update name and email. Shows verification status and resend link if email is unverified.</li>
  <li><strong>Update Password</strong> — Requires current password before accepting a new one.</li>
  <li><strong>Delete Account</strong> — Triggers a Bootstrap modal requiring password confirmation before permanent deletion.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  All form inputs are styled with a dark <code>#0f172a</code> background and subtle border, consistent with the overall dark theme.
</p>

